      "writtenOn": "2026-10-02T10:53:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It feels like waiting 5 min for a PR to be merges is a bit too much. In the current `mergePull` implementation we have a sleep of 5s with five attempts.\n\nThe problem I see here is that a pending merge (and I don\u0027t have a good grasp what could be the reason for that; maybe missing requirements / reviews?) could block pipeline processing during that time and with that the whole scheduler.",
      "revId": "2eac55882a566d7b6b8dc34854af98e215da429b",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ac85984_c318a71b",
        "filename": "zuul/driver/github/githubconnection.py",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 2372,
      "author": {
        "id": 1
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-02T14:29:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should not take long under normal circumstances, usually a few seconds.  The only reason we might not get an answer is due to an error on github\u0027s side, for example, if they drop the request entirely.\n\nI don\u0027t know why it might take longer than a few seconds.  I don\u0027t know if github has a fixed or scalable set of asynchronous workers to handle merges, but presumably they did this for a reason and expect that sometimes it might take a little while.  I think it\u0027s reasonable for us to have a generous timeout, so that if it takes 65 seconds to merge a pull request, we don\u0027t discard 6 hours of gate pipeline work.  Again, this is the time at which we give up waiting for a response from github, there\u0027s no way for us to influence the amount of time github takes.\n\nCompared to the normal synchronous merge -- I don\u0027t think the retry handler applies to the PUT request we send for a synchronous merge (it only handles GET 5xx errors).  Instead, I think we would rely on the requests session read timeout, which is 300.  With this setup, our timeout for waiting for the async pull is the same as a synchronous pull*.\n\n* (But we could spend longer in this method in the pathological case that github took 300s to return from the async status fetch call -- if that happened at the start of the process, then it\u0027s 300s.  If it happened at the end, then it\u0027s 300+300\u003d600.  But these calls are supposed to be instantaneous, so that\u0027s very unexpected.)",
      "parentUuid": "f0f5c5ca_b3353740",
      "revId": "2eac55882a566d7b6b8dc34854af98e215da429b",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "904a9742_6b15263a",
        "filename": "zuul/driver/github/githubconnection.py",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 2372,
      "author": {
        "id": 27582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-03T05:47:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m just thinking there is a good reason why Github made this an async merge API. But in Zuul we are turning it back into a synchronous merge operation.\n\nIn contrast the 300s for the sync merge is a request level timeout. We should not hit that as it\u0027s for exceptional case. But here the whole API seems to indicate that it can take longer to merge a PR.\n\nI think the main reason for why this is async is, that you can queue a PR for merge w/o the parent PR in the stack being ready. I guess Github will merge the PR when the parent becomes ready?!\n\nWith Zuul that (having a non merged parent PR) shouldn\u0027t happen as we merge PRs in order and if any of them fails we don\u0027t continue with that the rest of the stack.\n\nGiven that I\u0027d suggest to start with a lower timeout (60s?). I think in most cases where this takes longer there is something wrong and we should probably not wait 5min.",
      "parentUuid": "6ac85984_c318a71b",
      "revId": "2eac55882a566d7b6b8dc34854af98e215da429b",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97a1ca3c_ee2f5d87",
        "filename": "zuul/driver/github/githubconnection.py",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 2372,
      "author": {
        "id": 1
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T13:31:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I think we both agree that the reason the API is async is because it can be used to merge multiple commits at once.  That should not be an issue here since we merge commits in sequence.\n\nIf github can\u0027t merge a PR, it returns 400 immediately.  It doesn\u0027t just sits around waiting for it to become ready in the future.  There is a github feature for that, the merge queue, which is a pale imitation of zuul\u0027s gate pipeline.  But that is not this feature.\n\nGithub is trying to merge changes asap, but, since we could be making a request to merge a stack of 100 changes, presumably they just don\u0027t want to occupy a connection slot for that long.\n\nIn real-world testing, this is very fast.  So this timeout serves the same purpose of the other one: it is a timeout for an exceptional situation.  Just like we never expect to hit the 300s timeout waiting for a sync merge request, we also never expect to hit this 300s timeout waiting for an async merge request.",
      "parentUuid": "904a9742_6b15263a",
      "revId": "2eac55882a566d7b6b8dc34854af98e215da429b",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79137a7a_952b09c9",
        "filename": "zuul/driver/github/githubconnection.py",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 2372,
      "author": {
        "id": 27582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-09T09:53:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My concern is that we don\u0027t control the combination of Github features that a project can configure. I\u0027m fine with giving it a shot as-is, but I could imagine interesting edge cases in practice.\n\nI think we at least guard against using merge queues with stacked PRs as we\u0027d still fail the merge on the `enqueued` status.",
      "parentUuid": "97a1ca3c_ee2f5d87",
      "revId": "2eac55882a566d7b6b8dc34854af98e215da429b",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b778c572_60192a17",
        "filename": "zuul/driver/github/githubconnection.py",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 2372,
      "author": {
        "id": 1
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-09T13:09:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I agree that there could be some possible combination of features, now or in the future, that could surprise us.  And in that case, I agree that having a shorter timeout would be a good defence.  But at the moment at least, to the best of our ability, we have tried to make this behave as much like the sync path as possible.\n\nWe specifically guard against the use of merge queues by setting the \"merge_action\" to \"direct_merge\" below.",
      "parentUuid": "97a1ca3c_ee2f5d87",
      "revId": "2eac55882a566d7b6b8dc34854af98e215da429b",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
